02:03:07.690 --> 02:03:10.250
So you'll recall a couple of years ago, uh,

02:03:10.410 --> 02:03:14.610
the Earls Museum board, uh, requested that we take the depot property back.

02:03:15.090 --> 02:03:18.570
Uh, the city's always been the owner, but it was allocated to their early

02:03:18.570 --> 02:03:21.560
works board to, uh, to manage for us, uh,

02:03:21.770 --> 02:03:24.130
and the roundhouse specifically was used as an event center.

02:03:24.170 --> 02:03:26.780
I'm sure everyone here has been to events at the roundhouse.

02:03:27.150 --> 02:03:29.600
Uh, so in that, in that original agreement,

02:03:29.810 --> 02:03:32.940
uh, early works while the property came back under our control,

02:03:33.270 --> 02:03:35.090
uh, they would continue to operate their,

02:03:35.210 --> 02:03:37.890
the roundhouse through the end of 26, uh,

02:03:38.070 --> 02:03:40.440
to accommodate the reservations they'd already,

02:03:40.610 --> 02:03:42.600
uh, provided, uh, over that period of time.

02:03:43.360 --> 02:03:47.260
So you know we have been, uh, begun some of the master planning process

02:03:47.260 --> 02:03:50.400
and conducted several public meetings to get input from the public on the

02:03:50.400 --> 02:03:53.750
various ideas and and desires for uses of the overall property.

02:03:54.200 --> 02:03:57.310
Uh, one of the things that became very, very clear is that the public,

02:03:57.400 --> 02:04:00.840
uh, was asking that we allow it to continue to be an event center that it

02:04:00.840 --> 02:04:04.050
was, uh, highly used in a beloved space for that purpose,

02:04:04.400 --> 02:04:08.640
uh, and so we wanted to continue to be an event center as we did some analysis

02:04:08.640 --> 02:04:10.880
and spent some time working with the leadership at Early Works.

02:04:11.450 --> 02:04:12.690
Uh, it's our recommendation.

02:04:12.700 --> 02:04:15.590
It's actually better to allow them to continue to operate that specific

02:04:15.590 --> 02:04:16.410
building for that purpose.

02:04:16.490 --> 02:04:18.970
They already have employees, uh, that are,

02:04:19.010 --> 02:04:21.150
that are dedicated to that, uh, to that function.

02:04:21.370 --> 02:04:22.410
They know the facility well.

02:04:22.490 --> 02:04:25.770
They do it very efficiently, and the alternative to us trying to have public

02:04:25.770 --> 02:04:28.060
works or, I mean, Parks and recreation do it,

02:04:28.330 --> 02:04:30.440
uh, we think would be actually much more expensive,

02:04:30.610 --> 02:04:34.250
uh, and so it, it works well to let them just continue to operate as they

02:04:34.250 --> 02:04:34.640
have.

02:04:35.200 --> 02:04:39.040
Uh, we did, uh, spend some time looking at the condition of the building,

02:04:39.320 --> 02:04:41.840
uh, and specifically there are maintenance issues and stuff that we would

02:04:41.840 --> 02:04:43.720
have to undertake, and they've asked us to do that.

02:04:43.760 --> 02:04:47.990
And so what this does, one is it, it, it reverses the decision for them

02:04:47.990 --> 02:04:50.690
to give the roundhouse back to us at the end of this calendar year.

02:04:50.720 --> 02:04:53.200
