02:41:49.340 --> 02:41:53.260
into the Meridian Street extension of the Quigley district has stripped

02:41:53.260 --> 02:41:55.700
that fundamental right away from our neighbors.

02:41:55.980 --> 02:41:57.950
This is not a new conflict.

02:41:58.130 --> 02:42:02.350
The city's legal friction with this quarter stretches all the way back to

02:42:02.530 --> 02:42:04.820
a major municipal court trial on May.

02:42:04.960 --> 02:42:12.310
28, 2003, following a wave of environmental noise citations for 23 years,

02:42:12.350 --> 02:42:14.310
residents have begged for relief.

02:42:14.790 --> 02:42:18.150
When this council amended the noise ordinance on December 2,

02:42:18.350 --> 02:42:24.670
2021 with a narrow 3 to 2 vote, it was openly framed as a temporary experimental

02:42:24.670 --> 02:42:25.290
trial.

02:42:25.830 --> 02:42:29.610
Over two decades of data have given us the definitive answer.

02:42:29.910 --> 02:42:32.670
The experiment on Meridian Street has failed.

02:42:33.340 --> 02:42:38.100
The city has already taken the primary venue in this corridor to court at

02:42:38.100 --> 02:42:43.140
least twice over noise violations, yet the disruptions are escalating.

02:42:43.400 --> 02:42:48.260
For example, this Friday, tomorrow, the venue is hosting Hell's Bells,

02:42:48.510 --> 02:42:52.020
an ACDC tribute band on an outdoor patio.

02:42:52.670 --> 02:42:57.590
The heavy, low frequency base and stadium level volume cannot be contained

02:42:57.590 --> 02:42:59.910
by a simple patio barrier.

02:43:00.270 --> 02:43:04.510
Furthermore, the city's current enforcement tools are technically unequipped

02:43:04.510 --> 02:43:05.320
to handle it.

02:43:05.710 --> 02:43:10.630
Standard decibel meters filter out low frequencies and completely fail to

02:43:10.630 --> 02:43:11.790
